<h2>Decision Tree</h2>
<p>The decision tree is a set of rules detailed below that are used to determine if a project is likely to maintain is
    preservation status thorugh the set forcast date inside of the report section.
    <a>The rules were devloped between a joint efford between Roberta Rubin, and Jameer Gomez-Santos </a>
</p>

<h3>Decision Tree Rules</h3>
<div>
    <ul>
        <ul>
            <li>LIHTC Rule: If the <strong>"LIHTC_PIS" or "LIHTC_Alloc"</strong>field from the LIHTC tab (aka
                "LIHTCPUB_archive" table) is less than 30 years from the forecast cuttoff date, then the project will
                marked as preserved.</li>
                <li>If the project recvied state LIHTC funding, the decsion tree will suggest the project be preserved if
                    the forecast date is is within 45 years of the date LIHTC was awarded due to state LIHTC funding having
                    a 45 year minimum term. This is evulated by checking the <strong>"State LIHTC Awarded"</strong> and
                    subsequent awarded date fields in the DHCD_Archive table (EOHLC tab).
                </li>

            </ul>
            >
            <li>Rule 2, PRAC & 202s: If a project is identified a section 202 or PRAC/811 project, the decision tree will
                suggest the project be preserved. This is because 202/811 projects are required to be owned by a nonprofit
                and serve a sensitive population, and PRAC projects are required to be preserved by HUD.</li>
                <a>The decision tree evaluates if a project is 202 or PRAC by:</a>
                <ui>
                    <ol>
                        <li>If the <strong>"Program_Type_Group_Code"</strong> field in the
                            MF_Assistance_and_Sec8_Contracts_archive (AKA HUD Contract tab) table contains "202" or "PRAC", the
                            project is considered a 202 or PRAC project accordingly.</li>
                            <li>If the <strong>property_catagory_name</strong> or <strong>"property_financing_type"</strong> fields
                                in the MF_Properties_with_Assistance_and_Sec8_Contracts_archive (AKA HUD Propert tab) contains
                                202/811 or PRAC, the project is considered a 202 or PRAC project accordingly.</li>
                            </ol>
                        </ui>
                        
                        <li>
                            Override Rule: If a projects <strong>"Ar Risk Date Override" is before the override date, then the decision tree will suggest that the project remains preserved </strong>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
    
                </div>

